# jetson_pins.env -- PURPOSE: the pinned PyTorch wheels of the Jetson (arm64) image, read by `jetson.sh image build`.
# The Jetson torch wheels come from the Jetson AI Lab index for JetPack 6 / CUDA 12.6 (the team's own
# requirements_jetson.txt uses the same index). A wheel re-published under the same version number once needed
# libcudss.so.0, which JetPack 6.2 lacks (HIL_DESIGN.md risk 18), so the exact files are recorded here by their
# sha256. Read from the index page on 2026-10-31 (curl .../+simple/torch/ and .../+simple/torchvision/); the torch
# hash starts with 62a1beee9f2f1470, as the design review read it.
# They are enforced once docker/Dockerfile accepts TORCH_SHA256 / TORCHVISION_SHA256 (PATCH P2 in the report);
# until then the build uses the version numbers only and selftest's "import torch" is the check.
TORCH_INDEX_URL=https://pypi.jetson-ai-lab.io/jp6/cu126/+simple/
TORCH_VERSION=2.8.0
TORCHVISION_VERSION=0.23.0
TORCH_WHEEL=torch-2.8.0-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl
TORCH_SHA256=62a1beee9f2f147076a974d2942c90060c12771c94740830327cae705b2595fc
TORCHVISION_WHEEL=torchvision-0.23.0-cp310-cp310-linux_aarch64.whl
TORCHVISION_SHA256=907c4c1933789645ebb20dd9181d40f8647978e6bd30086ae7b01febb937d2d1
